								<div class="title" id="post-title-3605615">
																		Author Post - I get the feelin&#039; this is never gonna end
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decibelles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2005044); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2005044&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608782399" alt="Decibelles" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2005044)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decibelles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2005044); return false;" >Decibelles</a></span> <span class="odate time_1506889974 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Oct 2017 20:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3605615">
									

<p>Thanks to the following:</p>
<ul>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-great-hippo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3122708); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3122708&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506890563" alt="The Great Hippo" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3122708)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-great-hippo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3122708); return false;">The Great Hippo</a></span> for essentially being an enormous in-depth critiquer and editor. This tale was already great before I showed him, but it became the exact product I envisioned in my head after we finished.</li>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modern-erasmus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3129691); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3129691&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506890563" alt="Modern_Erasmus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3129691)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modern-erasmus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3129691); return false;">Modern_Erasmus</a></span> for looking it over and suggesting to elaborate on a certain aspect of the story that I will do in future installments.</li>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/taffeta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2221240); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2221240&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506890563" alt="Taffeta" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2221240)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/taffeta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2221240); return false;">Taffeta</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kinchtheknifeblade" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1345012); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1345012&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506890563" alt="kinchtheknifeblade" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1345012)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kinchtheknifeblade" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1345012); return false;">kinchtheknifeblade</a></span> for looking it over.</li>
</ul>
<p>This is a tale about two characters I've created and am now expanding upon. The Japanese site already beat me to writing one of them and Scantron beat me to the other but this is them in the physical world, more realized. Also, they play noisy dance-punk music like Death From Above 1979, except more raw and gutter-y.</p>
<p>What I want to expand upon in future installments is the setting these two are in. Specifically, they live in Rocinha, Brazil. I didn't wanna make up a favela after talking about it with Erasmus. I think it's important for me to build upon how characters live in Brazil in the Foundationverse, since being Brazilian is a big part of my heritage and influenced my life in a very positive, impactful way.</p>
<p>Also; I debated whether or not to keep their exchange at the end of the first part. I figure I should. Their interactions are loosely based on the dynamic a trans guy friend and I have. We're both gay and we both call each other shit like that. I think it's funny.</p>
<p><strong>ONE THING TO KEEP IN MIND!!</strong> This is actually important for me to emphasize, but despite me writing everything entirely in English, you should assume they are speaking Portuguese to each other. There are a couple words I couldn't find a good way to translate into English and keep their meaning, but they are speaking Portuguese here. Why would they be speaking English to each other?</p>
<p>Stuff I listened to while writing: Death From Above 1979's <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Vb8pI82jIE">You're A Woman, I'm a Machine</a>, <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FNbVvE-u-vk">The Physical World</a> (the song of which I got the title of this tale from), and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLCWXIh7vWQTKFj5-7wCiWla169dnYRZ4m">Heads Up</a>, as well as Dean Blunt's <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PJNHQ8gUIZc">untitled unmastered unheard unfinished unrehearsed unplugged un...</a>.</p>
<p>The chatlog is a throwback to one of my first tales on the site, <a href="/anime-is-art-too-guys">Anime Is Art Too, Guys</a>.</p>

							</div>

								
