			<div class="content" id="post-content-3605618">
									

<p>I really enjoyed the dialogue here, the sparseness of it. Sometimes that can work against the piece but it felt Hemingway-esque in the right way here. The chat interlude didn't feel intrusive and the interactions of the characters felt very natural and real. I think after the chatlog you wrap it up a bit too quickly, I would've liked to maybe see some more imagery mined from the amplifier bursting and while I like the last scene I think more of a comedown from what came before would do this piece well. I still enjoyed myself, so +1</p>

